# World 2's chip budget (SPEC 11, "World 2, slice 2"): the DPS logo of the boot splash (37,456 bytes and its two
# copper lists, 47 KB) stayed allocated for the whole game; it is freed when world 2 loads (display off, the floppy
# load already runs with the OS on). The game prints the chip free to the byte once world 2 is loaded:
# a500 97 KB before, 138 KB with the radar site's block (slice A), 137 with the windsock (B), 130 with the deck's art (C, 7,632
# bytes: 133,656 measured): the check is 128 KB or more (measured minus 2 KB; the a1200 has 1.2 MB).
# World 1 keeps its 105 KB (nothing is freed there).
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x04
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 400
wait 120
expect-serial "AGK w2 chipfree=(12[89]|1[3-9][0-9]|[2-9][0-9][0-9]|[0-9]{4})\b"
expect-no-serial "AGK ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-min-chip-free 96
